160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Throughout the course of the project, various situations and challenges were observed and addressed. Some final observations and recommendations include:)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Persistent Errors: Some errors identified in earlier stages were not corrected in the current stage. It is crucial to address these issues to improve software quality and prevent them from accumulating in future stages.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Data Validation: Issues were identified in data validation, particularly in the entry of email addresses and invalid characters. It is recommended to enhance the validation logic to cover all possible error scenarios and ensure the integrity of entered data.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (User Interface Consistency: Inconsistencies were observed in the presentation of the user interface across different browsers. It is important to align the design layout with the final implementation to ensure consistency in the presentation and functionality of the system across all browsers.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Database Integration: The management system is not connected to the database, which affects the integrity and modularity of the system. This issue must be resolved to ensure efficient data management and enable the execution of critical vulnerability tests.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
